<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balša II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1385">1385</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balša II was a lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> of the Balšić family, which took control of the land around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-skadar">Lake Skadar</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>'s death. He ruled Zeta from 1378 and expanded into Albania, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Valona</a> by marriage and seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> in 1385. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-thopia">Karl Thopia</a> called in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, who defeated and killed him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-savra">Battle of Savra</a> that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balsa-ii.jpg" alt="Balša II" width="320" height="553" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petarrc13 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bal%C5%A1i%C4%87_noble_family_banner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
